# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 1: Map classical inputs to a quantum problem {#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"
msgstr "Langkah 1. Petakan input klasik kepada masalah kuantum {#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Choose a backend {#choose-a-backend}"
msgstr "Pilih backend {#choose-a-backend}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To detect errors during the circuit, we need to choose a backend that has access to the `MidCircuitMeasure` method (see the [documentation](/guides/execute-dynamic-circuits#mid-circuit-measurements)).\n"
msgstr "Untuk mengesan ralat semasa litar, kita perlu memilih backend yang mempunyai akses kepada kaedah `MidCircuitMeasure` (lihat [dokumentasi](/guides/execute-dynamic-circuits#mid-circuit-measurements)).\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Build a sequence of bit-flip stabilizer circuits implementing multiple rounds of error detection and correction {#build-a-sequence-of-bit-flip-stabilizer-circuits-implementing-multiple-rounds-of-error-detection-and-correction}"
msgstr "Bina satu siri litar stabiliser bit-flip yang melaksanakan berbilang pusingan pengesanan dan pembetulan ralat {#build-a-sequence-of-bit-flip-stabilizer-circuits-implementing-multiple-rounds-of-error-detection-and-correction}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The bit-flip code is among the simplest examples of a stabilizer code. It protects the state against a single bit-flip (X) error on any of the encoding qubits. Consider the action of bit-flip error $X$, which maps $|0\\rangle \\rightarrow |1\\rangle$ and $|1\\rangle \\rightarrow |0\\rangle$ on any of our qubits, then we have $\\epsilon = \\{E_0, E_1, E_2 \\} = \\{IIX, IXI, XII\\}$. The code requires five qubits: three are used to encode the protected state (the \"data qubits\"), and the remaining two are used as stabilizer measurement ancillas.\n"
msgstr "Kod bit-flip adalah antara contoh kod penstabil yang paling mudah. Ia melindungi keadaan daripada ralat bit-flip (X) tunggal pada mana-mana qubit pengekodan. Pertimbangkan tindakan ralat bit-flip $X$, yang memetakan $|0\\rangle \\rightarrow |1\\rangle$ dan $|1\\rangle \\rightarrow |0\\rangle$ pada mana-mana qubit kita, maka kita ada $\\epsilon = \\{E_0, E_1, E_2 \\} = \\{IIX, IXI, XII\\}$. Kod ini memerlukan lima qubit: tiga digunakan untuk mengekodkan keadaan yang dilindungi (\"qubit data\"), dan dua yang lain digunakan sebagai ancilla pengukuran penstabil.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Below you will build circuits that (1) prepare the data qubits in the logical $|\\bar{1} \\rangle$ state, then (2) run multiple cycles of a $5 \\mu s$ delay followed by error correction (including reset of the syndrome qubits), and (3) read out the state of the data qubits.\n"
msgstr "Di bawah anda akan membina litar yang (1) menyediakan qubit data dalam keadaan logik $|\\bar{1} \\rangle$, kemudian (2) menjalankan berbilang kitaran kelewatan $5 \\mu s$ diikuti oleh pembetulan ralat (termasuk set semula qubit sindrom), dan (3) membaca keadaan qubit data.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We will also test the lifetime of the $|1\\rangle$ state without using error correction by including three reference qubits that we prepare in the $|1\\rangle$ state, leave idle, and then read out.\n"
msgstr "Kami juga akan menguji jangka hayat keadaan $|1\\rangle$ tanpa menggunakan pembetulan ralat dengan menyertakan tiga qubit rujukan yang kami sediakan dalam keadaan $|1\\rangle$, biarkan terbiar, dan kemudian dibaca.\n"

